From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: natemu <natemu@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] FEXCore: slice1 I6 x87 reduced precision: state, FIST, FSW

Under fexc_slice1 only (x87 in FEX's reduced-precision mode, which fexc sets
for slice1).

- x87StackOptimizationPass: always the slow path, and every lowered op flushes
  and drops its caches, so the x87 state (mm[], TOP, the abridged tag word) is
  in the guest-state page at every instruction boundary (a fault or stop
  anywhere sees it exact) and no register pressure builds up (slice1 admits no
  spill area); TOP is masked to 0..7 on load (a guest-state byte the guest can
  reach); ST(i) is accessed as LoadContextIndexed/StoreContextIndexed
  (`add x0, x28, xI, lsl #4; ldr|str dN, [x0, #mm]`), not as a guest memory op.
- X87F64.cpp FISTF64: x86's FIST/FISTP/FISTTP. Round by the FPCR (frintx: PE
  when inexact) or truncate (fcvtzs), convert at 64 bits, and store the
  integer indefinite for a NaN or a value outside the operand size's range
  (Arm saturates; FEX stored the low half of a 64-bit conversion for m16);
  flag-free. IE from FPSR.IOC or, for m16/m32 range, FEX's IE byte; m16/m32
  round without a flag and set PE in FEX's PE byte only for a stored inexact
  result (x86 raises IE alone out of range); both bytes after the store.
- x87StackOptimizationPass: x87 stack faults with their masked response (SDM
  Vol.1 8.5.1.1; every exception stays masked): a read of an empty register
  gives the QNaN indefinite (underflow), a push onto a non-empty one loads it
  (overflow); IE and SF set and C1 = 1 / 0 before the next instruction (after
  this one's store); a register written is always marked valid (an underflow
  fills its destination). FXAM reads ST(0) from the page directly (no fault).
- x87StackOptimizationPass: C1 = overflow on every push and 0 for FCHS/FABS;
  an arithmetic result after a stack underflow is the indefinite even beside
  a NaN operand; FST/FSTP m64 quiets an SNaN with IE (integer code).
- X87F64.cpp FLDF64: FLD m64 is a multiply by 1.0 (SNaN quieted with IE,
  denormal DE, exact otherwise under the x87 FPCR); FCOMIF64: C1 = 0 for
  FCOMI/FUCOMI(P).
- x87StackOptimizationPass: FCHS and FABS as sign-bit operations (Arm FNEG and
  FABS leave a NaN unchanged under FPCR.AH = 1; x87's flip or clear its sign).
- X87.cpp X87FXAM: x86's classes of a double (empty, NaN, infinity, zero,
  normal; a denormal double is a normal 80-bit value), C1 the sign; flag-free.
- X87.cpp ReconstructFSW_Helper: FSW's exception flags from the x87 exception
  word, FEX's IE, PE and SF bytes (FPSR order, filled by the JIT's x87 wrapper in shim/fexc_sites.inc).
- JITClass.h: the wrapper's declarations.
